### The reported failure, reproduced and diagnosed on the user's own file

Model: qwen3.5:9b-q4_K_M   File: test-shamsu/test1/js/main.js
582 lines / 18,917 chars - over the 6,963 write cap, so a whole-file rewrite is
refused and the model must edit in place.

THE FILE'S ACTUAL DEFECT WAS NOT A SYNTAX ERROR. `node --check` passes on all
seven JS files. Four functions are declared TWICE:

    handleQuit             line 81 (nested)  and 535
    handleMouseMove        line 122          and 547
    handleClickToShoot     line 135          and 573
    handlePauseMenuAction  line 178 (e)      and 517 (action)

In JavaScript the later declaration silently wins, and no parser can see it.
index.html also loads ONLY js/main.js - the other six files are never loaded.

--- BASELINE, before any fix (4 runs) --------------------------------------
run A  died at round 5, Ollama 500: malformed tool call XML
run B  24 rounds, 319s, changed NOTHING
run C  24 rounds, correct
run D  24 rounds, correct

Run B's transcript gave the cause:

    patch_file      x4  -> "old_string not found"
    replace_symbol  x2  -> "replace_symbol needs a filepath, a symbol and content"
                           symbol  = 'handlePauseMenuAction(action)'
                           content = '\n'

The model was RIGHT and the tool would not let it. It had found the duplicate
and was deleting it by replacing it with nothing - the correct move, and the
only one available, since patch_file would need the exact text of a 30-line
body. Two defects refused that one call: the symbol carried its signature, and
empty content read as a missing argument.

--- WHERE THE ROUNDS WENT (4 runs) -----------------------------------------
             read_file   contract_assert_pass FAILED   patch_file
    t1          13                 3                    1 ok / 1 fail
    t2           9                 6                    3 ok
    t3          13                 7                    1 ok
    t4          11                 7                    0 ok / 4 fail

23 contract failures - more than every other failure combined. 17 of them
carried the RIGHT id under a name the code does not read:

    7x assertion_index='a01'   6x contract_id   2x claim   1x claim_id
    1x assertion              2x evidence only  4x no arguments

--- AFTER THE FIXES (3 runs) -----------------------------------------------
run 1  WRONG    24 rounds   lost handleMouseMove entirely (2 -> 0 definitions)
run 2  CORRECT  24 rounds
run 3  CORRECT  24 rounds

Run 1 was a REGRESSION I introduced: patch removed copy 1 (2->1, allowed),
then replace_symbol with empty content removed copy 2 (1->0, unguarded).
replace_symbol had been exempted from the erasure guard on the assumption that
_members_lost covered it - it does not, it asks what vanished from INSIDE a
replaced symbol. Fixed in a574b46; the exact sequence is now refused at step 2.

--- WHAT DID NOT HOLD UP ---------------------------------------------------
The read-loop looked like a consistent 3-in-3 leak (3, 13, 12 blocked reads)
and did not reproduce (8, 1, 3) on the next three runs of the same code against
the same file. Dynamic pruning was built for it, is correct, fires only when
the model really loops - and changed the round count not at all: 24/24/24
before and after. Rounds were 24 in every one of the seven runs taken.

CONCLUSION. The tool defects are real, deterministic and fixed. The efficiency
question was being answered from 3-run samples and was chasing variance both
times it was asked. That is what the telemetry in 4d117b7 exists to end.
